# BIKIE Project Rules

- Read `CLAUDE.md` and relevant `.docs/*` before non-trivial work.
- Audit and characterize behavior before architectural refactoring.
- Migrate one bounded context at a time; never perform a repository-wide file move.
- Preserve existing API routes, payloads, status codes, auth behavior, and mobile compatibility.
- Enforce `UI → Route → Application Service → Port → Repository/Adapter`.
- No Prisma outside `packages/database`; no vendor SDK in domain/application business logic.
- Cross-module consumers import only a module's public API.
- Keep Next.js Route Handlers in `apps/web` unless a new ADR changes ADR-001.
- Use feature flags for risky parallel implementations, with owner and removal condition.
- Add tests before deleting compatibility paths.
- Never add secrets; document variable names only in `.env.example`.
- Update tasks, roadmap, changelog, and architecture/API/ADR docs as required.
